#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "CAP-MODELS Governed analytical models"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Predictive models, such as early-warning flags, that advise people, are reproducible, and are checked for unequal error before release."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Layer L3 · domain: product · depends on: [CAP-TRANSFORMATION]{1}, [CAP-REVIEW]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Use predictive models, such as early-warning flags, without letting them decide about people."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "A model that flags a child is a statement about that child; it must be reproducible, explainable, checked for unequal error across groups, and always weighed by a person ([P9]{1}, [P10]{2})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "A model registry; deterministic batch scoring."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Flags delivered into the review queue with their signals."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Prefer interpretable models; an early-warning signal that a teacher cannot understand will not be acted on well."
msgstr ""

