msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "CAP-MODELS.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "A model is versioned with its training data pinned, scoring is deterministic, and every score records the model version."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Scoring a fixed input twice gives identical scores with the version attached."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "CAP-MODELS.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "A risk flag is advice to a person and never triggers an automatic action on a learner or staff member; the person's decision is recorded with attribution."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "No downstream process consumes a flag except the review queue."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "CAP-MODELS.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Performance and error rates are reported by sex, area, disability and other declared equity dimensions before release and on a schedule; a model whose disparity exceeds its declared bound is not released.{1}*Example:* An early-warning model flags boys three times as often as girls with the same actual dropout rate; the disparity exceeds its declared bound, so it is not released."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "The release record holds the disaggregated evaluation and the bound."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "CAP-MODELS.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Each flag shows the signals that raised it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "The review view lists the contributing signals for each flag."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "CAP-MODELS.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "Before a model that scores learners is released, it is assessed against the UNICEF Guidance on AI and Children, and the assessment is kept with the release."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-models.md
msgid "The release record holds the assessment."
msgstr ""

